# ChefFlow SPA environment — copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
# Vite exposes only variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.

# Required: Clerk frontend (publishable) key. Get from clerk.com → Dashboard
# → API Keys. Use the live (pk_live_…) key in production, test (pk_test_…) in dev.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_replace_me

# Required: which LLM transport to use.
#   "proxy" — production. SPA calls /api/llm/* on the Cloudflare Worker,
#             which holds the LLM credentials server-side.
#   "groq"  — local dev with a bring-your-own Groq key (see VITE_GROQ_API_KEY).
VITE_LLM_MODE=proxy

# Optional: only used when VITE_LLM_MODE=groq. Get from console.groq.com.
# Never set this in a production build — keys must stay server-side.
# VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional: Google Maps Places API key for event-location autocomplete.
# If unset, the autocomplete dropdown just doesn't appear (free-text still works).
# Create at console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials, then
# restrict the key to "Places API (New)" + your origin.
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional: Sentry DSN for client-side error reporting. Leave blank to skip
# Sentry initialisation entirely (the code is a no-op without a DSN).
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Optional: version string baked into bug-report mailto and Sentry release tag.
# Defaults to "dev". Set this in CI/CD to the commit SHA or release tag.
# VITE_APP_VERSION=
